//
// Kept here because campaign dirs live under ~/tmp, which is tmpfs on
// every box in the fleet — a reboot loses the only copy.
//
// Untriaged. Note the shape: `count(...)` over a `let rec` whose
// recursive arm is `n - f(n - 1)`, alongside an `array::iter` feeding a
// guard that is never actually reachable (`select i64:-1` with an
// `i64:0` arm). The lost event is the THIRD of four, so whatever it is
// needs two prior fires to set it up.
//
// ROOT-CAUSED 2026-08-10: the DEPTH-TRIP ABORT SEAM vs the caller's
// operand-cache ride. x iterates 0,2,0,4 -> f(-1), f(1), f(-1), f(3).
// f(-1) descends to the 256 limit and trips. On current HEAD both
// traces start at epoch 2 (the header's epoch-1 event was the
// pre-minimization mutant's, whose array began [1,...]):
//   epoch 1, f(-1) FRESH: interp delivers the settled tainted bottom
//     (the 2026-07-23 abort-seam ruling) and the standing callsite's
//     `n - f(n-1)` has NO ride history — no emission. Kernel aborts
//     the invocation ("produced no value"). AGREE, coincidentally.
//   epoch 2/4, f(1)/f(3): terminate normally, frame 2 last returns 0
//     (f(0)) resp. 1. AGREE.
//   epoch 3, f(-1) AGAIN: interp — the trip taints the inner call,
//     but the OUTERMOST activation's subtraction rides frame 2's
//     prior success per the 000004 ruling (bottom = no event, prior
//     rides): -1 - 0 = -1, EMITS. Kernel — depth trip is a GENUINE
//     whole-kernel abort (emit contract list: interrupt poll, depth
//     trip, ...), the invocation is discarded wholesale, and the
//     independently-computable `n - <cached>` never runs. LOST FIRE.
//
// So the 07-23 "delivery matches the kernel's abort-to-placeholder
// seam" holds only when the trip has no upstream ride history. The
// fix needs two pieces, the second of which is the known
// infrastructure gap: (1) a callee depth trip should deliver the
// tainted placeholder AT THE TRIPPING CALL SITE (as a pended DynCall
// does) instead of aborting the kernel; (2) the caller-frame operand
// taint cache that would then ride sits in a NON-ROOT callee body —
// the honor-gated "region-root active, elsewhere inert" residual
// (taint-cache-callee-jul2026), the same wall the fire-gate witness
// hit (dyncall-fire-gate-aug2026). Triaged, OPEN: gated on the
// ASPIRE value-resident/taint-cache-in-callee work; keep here until
// that lands, then this becomes its pin.
//
// bisect: fusion/JIT bug (interp != jit)
// interp: Trace(Trace { epochs: [Epoch { events: [(1, I64(0)), (2, I64(1)), (3, I64(-1)), (4, I64(2))], capped: false }], stdout: [] })
// jit:    Trace(Trace { epochs: [Epoch { events: [(1, I64(0)), (2, I64(1)), (4, I64(2))], capped: false }], stdout: [] })
// mutant: {let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2, i64:0, i64:4]); let m = x / i64:3; let f = |k| select i64:-1 {i64:0 if m == i64:0 => i64:1, _ => i64:1}; let m = count(let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => i64:0, _ => n - f(n - i64:1)}); f(x - i64:1)}
